# Marks

A parameter written `^T` is written in place, and `^^T` takes its value.
A receiver `^self` or `^^self` does the same; `a & b` and `a && b` are
operators, and so is a bare & in prose.

```jet
grow: fn(items: ^[Int]) { items.push(4) }
seal: fn(buf: ^^[Int]) -> Int { buf.len() }
both: fn(a: Bool, b: Bool) -> Bool { a && b }
```

```rust
fn grow(items: &mut Vec<i32>) { items.push(4) }
fn len(items: &[i32]) -> usize { items.len() }
```
